    "description": "Natural Specimen Collection\nGeode and Mineral Rock Lot\nAmethyst, Pyrite, and Quartz\nVarying Dimensions\nNatural and Enhanced Specimens\nThis diverse collection of six geological specimens features a range of natural and treated minerals. The set includes a notable amethyst cluster with embedded pyrite cubes mounted on a glass base, originally sourced from Park City, Utah. Also included is a translucent amethyst crystal point with a \"Made in Brazil\" provenance, and a vibrant red titanium-coated aura quartz specimen featuring a high-luster iridescent finish.\nIncludes large milky quartz and yellow quartz rough specimens measuring approximately 3.5 inches\nFeatures natural amethyst druzy with cubic pyrite inclusions from a known Utah locality\nSet contains a mix of raw mineral points, clusters, and a smooth polished accent stone\nCondition:\nVery good overall condition. Natural specimens exhibit expected geological textures and raw edges. The aura quartz coating is uniform and bright. The mounted Utah specimen is securely attached to its glass display base. Total lot weight is 1.0 lb.",
